.TH SDL_sscanf 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_sscanf \- This works exactly like sscanf() but doesn\(aqt require access to a C runtime.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "int SDL_sscanf(const char *text, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a string, matching a format string, converting each \(aq%\(aq item and storing it to pointers provided through variable arguments\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I text
the string to scan\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I fmt
a printf-style format string\[char46] Must not be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I ...
a list of pointers to values to be filled in with scanned items\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of items that matched the format string\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

